<% content_for :title, "Essays | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-essays-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-essays-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-essays-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-essays-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ESSAYS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>SHIT I'VE</span>
        <span>THOUGHT</span>
        <span>ABOUT.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-essays-intro">
        RECOVERY. BIPOLAR. ADDICTION.<br>
        LIFE. AND WHATEVER THE FUCK<br>
        ELSE ENDED UP ON THE PAGE.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="essays-intro-section">

    <div class="essays-section-number">
      01 / ESSAYS
    </div>

    <div class="essays-intro-content">

      <h2>
        SOMETIMES<br>
        I NEED MORE<br>
        THAN A BULLET POINT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Some things fit neatly into a coping skill, a definition,
        or a list of things to try.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some shit doesn't.
      </p>

      <p>
        These are the longer thoughts: recovery, mental illness,
        addiction, identity, consequences, starting over, and trying
        to understand what the hell happened without pretending
        there's always a clean answer.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ESSAY GRID -->
  <section class="essays-library">

    <div class="essays-library-heading">

      <p>02 / FROM THE NOTEBOOK</p>

      <h2>
        READ<br>
        SOMETHING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Thoughts from somewhere between figuring shit out
        and realizing I probably never completely will.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="essays-grid">

      <!-- ESSAY 01 -->
      <article class="essay-card essay-card-pink">

        <p class="essay-card-number">01</p>

        <p class="essay-card-category">
          RECOVERY
        </p>

        <h3>
          STARTING<br>
          OVER.
        </h3>

        <p>
          What happens when the life you thought you were building
          doesn't look anything like the life you're standing in now?
        </p>

        <span>COMING SOON</span>

      </article>


      <!-- ESSAY 02 -->
      <article class="essay-card essay-card-yellow">

        <p class="essay-card-number">02</p>

        <p class="essay-card-category">
          ADDICTION
        </p>

        <h3>
          THE STORY<br>
          WE TELL<br>
          OURSELVES.
        </h3>

        <p>
          The explanations, excuses, bargains, and absolutely
          convincing bullshit that can make a terrible idea
          sound reasonable.
        </p>

        <span>COMING SOON</span>

      </article>


      <!-- ESSAY 03 -->
      <article class="essay-card essay-card-purple">

        <p class="essay-card-number">03</p>

        <p class="essay-card-category">
          BIPOLAR
        </p>

        <h3>
          WHICH PART<br>
          WAS ME?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Trying to understand identity when moods, episodes,
          impulses, choices, and consequences all get tangled together.
        </p>

        <span>COMING SOON</span>

      </article>


      <!-- ESSAY 04 -->
      <article class="essay-card essay-card-black">

        <p class="essay-card-number">04</p>

        <p class="essay-card-category">
          LIFE
        </p>

        <h3>
          WHAT NOW?
        </h3>

        <p>
          Because eventually the crisis ends, the dust settles,
          and you're still standing there with a life that needs living.
        </p>

        <span>COMING SOON</span>

      </article>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- WHY WRITE -->
  <section class="essays-write-section">

    <div class="essays-section-number">
      03 / WHY WRITE?
    </div>

    <div class="essays-write-content">

      <h2>
        GET IT<br>
        OUT OF<br>
        YOUR HEAD.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Thoughts can sound airtight when they're bouncing around
        inside your own brain.
      </p>

      <p>
        Writing makes you slow them down enough to actually look at them.
        Sometimes you find insight. Sometimes you find a pattern.
        Sometimes you discover that something you've been telling yourself
        sounds completely fucking ridiculous once it's on paper.
      </p>

      <div class="essays-callout">
        <p>
          YOU DON'T HAVE TO KNOW<br>
          WHAT YOU THINK BEFORE<br>
          YOU START WRITING.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PROMPTS -->
  <section class="essays-prompts">

    <div class="essays-section-number">
      04 / YOUR TURN
    </div>

    <div class="essays-prompts-content">

      <h2>
        WRITE YOUR<br>
        OWN FUCKING<br>
        ESSAY.
      </h2>

      <div class="essay-prompt-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>
            What is something I believe about myself that I have
            never seriously questioned?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>
            What did alcohol, substances, or impulsive behavior
            actually do for me?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>
            What am I still angry about?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>
            What am I afraid will happen if my life actually changes?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>
            What have I survived that I rarely give myself credit for?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>
            Who am I when I'm not defining myself by my worst decisions?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>07</span>
          <p>
            What does the life I'm trying to build actually look like?
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="essays-ending">

    <p class="essays-ending-small">
      YOU DON'T NEED A CONCLUSION YET.
    </p>

    <h2>
      JUST START<br>
      FUCKING<br>
      WRITING.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Sometimes the point isn't finding the answer.
      It's finally asking the question.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "essays-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>